            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0212" n="96" xml:id="pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/46.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Calhoun to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In reply to May 16. Sheng Kung Pao is specially entrusted by Prince Regent with
                    work of improving river conditions in famine district. He will gladly accept
                    offer of Red Cross to furnish American engineer. He hopes the latter will come
                    as soon as possible. He will organize corps of necessary assistants. Situation
                    requires prompt attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
